components.tokens:
[data-verify="unverified"] { border-left: 4px solid transparent; background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, color-mix(in oklab, var(--text) 42%, transparent) 0 2px, transparent 2px 5px); background-repeat:no-repeat; background-size:4px 100%; background-position:left top; padding-left: calc(var(--gutter) - 4px); }
.fd-unverified__tag { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:var(--fs-12); letter-spacing:.12em; padding:2px 7px; border-radius:var(--r-control); background:var(--bg-2); color:var(--text); border:1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--text) 55%, transparent); }
.fd-unverified__what { font-size:var(--fs-14); color:var(--text); }
.fd-unverified__settle { font-size:var(--fs-14); color:var(--muted); } and its <b> is mono --fs-12, uppercase, colour var(--dim).
.fd-u { text-decoration: underline dotted 1px; text-underline-offset:3px; text-decoration-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--text) 55%, transparent); cursor:help; } and .fd-u::after{content:" ?"; font-family:var(--font-mono); color:var(--dim)} so it is not a colour-only or hover-only signal.
No accent token appears anywhere in this component. That is the rule.
